# Line endings are NOT cosmetic in this repo.
#
# `hud/src/main.rs` carries guards that slice literal JS out of `hud/ui/index.html` by searching
# for markers like `const persist = ` … `;\n`. Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so
# a checkout on Windows rewrites every LF to CRLF — the marker becomes `;\r\n`, the search misses,
# and ten tests fail with "`const persist = ` must still contain `;`". The code is fine; the
# working tree was rewritten underneath it.
#
# starplatform never saw this because its CI is Linux-only. This repo builds on Windows — the
# platform the client actually ships on — so it is the first place the fragility shows up.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform makes checkouts deterministic and keeps them
# byte-identical to what is stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.msi  binary
